Although I don't doubt that ANY death one suffers with a good character is 
annoying, I think one can only justifiably complain that Fate has been cruel
when theree was little or nothing you yourself could have done to avoid death.
	In the case of the fellow slain by the giant beetle, for instance, he
should have been smart enough to just *drop* his 22 scrolls, or whatever,
kill the darned beetle, and then try sacrificing the unicorn (though no doubt
the priest probably would have killed him).
	No, injustice is what happened to me one time, when I was playing with
nurses...had an excellent character, but very low hit points.  So, with a
blindfold on to watch out for encroaching bad guys, I slip out of my skivvies
(including a shield of reflection) to get down and dirty with the nurse.  Still
had my amulet of life saving on, though.  But then, the game randomly generated
a black dragon two steps away.  Hmm...might be a problem...but I'm faster than
he...oh, no I'm not, 'cuz I haven't got the boots on.  He breathes, hits me,
I start to disintegrate.  The amulet saves me...but the very same bolt then
bounces off the wall behind me and kills me again, in the same turn!  Erg.
The nurse laughs discretely as my ghost swears bloody vengeance...

